# Module 1 — How the Web Talks: requests from the morning
# Open in VS Code with REST Client; click "Send Request" above each ###.
# The status each request returned is written as a comment under its title.
#
# GitHub is NOT called from this file: the lab shares one IP and GitHub allows
# 60 unauthenticated requests per hour per IP. Read GitHub responses from
# shared/offline-data/github/ (or the fixtures/ folder in the Student Pack).

@httpbin = https://httpbin.org
@jsonph = https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com

# =====================================================================
# Exercise 5 — the first five requests
# =====================================================================

### 1. GET with a query string (httpbin echoes it back) — expect 200
# Status: 200 OK — "args": {"course": "apis", "module": "1"}
GET {{httpbin}}/get?course=apis&module=1
Accept: application/json

### 2. What headers did my client send? — expect 200
# Status: 200 OK — User-Agent: vscode-restclient
GET {{httpbin}}/headers

### 3. Read one post — expect 200
# Status: 200 OK — userId 1, id 1
GET {{jsonph}}/posts/1

### 4. Create a post: a JSON body needs Content-Type and a blank line before the body — expect 201
# Status: 201 Created — "id": 101 (JSONPlaceholder pretends to save it)
POST {{jsonph}}/posts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Platform renewal",
  "body": "Lumina, 2021-2026",
  "userId": 1
}

### 5. Ask for something that does not exist — expect 404
# Status: 404 Not Found — body {}
GET {{jsonph}}/posts/9999

# =====================================================================
# Lab — API exploration log (results recorded in api/docs/api-exploration.md)
# =====================================================================

### L1. httpbin: GET /get with two query parameters — expect 200
# Status: 200 OK
GET {{httpbin}}/get?section=A&seat=12
Accept: application/json

### L2. httpbin: POST /post with a JSON body — expect 200 (httpbin echoes, it doesn't create)
# Status: 200 OK — the body comes back under "json"
POST {{httpbin}}/post
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "award": "Founders' Recognition for Commitment",
  "year": 2009
}

### L3. httpbin: a joke status code — expect 418
# Status: 418 I'm a teapot — the body is an ASCII teapot
GET {{httpbin}}/status/418

### L4. httpbin (own request): ask for 429 — expect 429
# Status: 429 Too Many Requests — empty body
GET {{httpbin}}/status/429

### L5. JSONPlaceholder: one user — expect 200
# Status: 200 OK — "name": "Leanne Graham"
GET {{jsonph}}/users/1

### L6. JSONPlaceholder: a filter in the query string — expect 200
# Status: 200 OK — 10 posts, all with "userId": 1
GET {{jsonph}}/posts?userId=1

### L7. JSONPlaceholder: PATCH only the title — expect 200
# Status: 200 OK — the whole post comes back with the new title
PATCH {{jsonph}}/posts/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Platform renewal (edited)"
}

### L8. JSONPlaceholder: DELETE one post — expect 200
# Status: 200 OK — body {} (many real APIs answer 204 No Content)
DELETE {{jsonph}}/posts/1

### L9. JSONPlaceholder (own request): another user's todos — expect 200
# Status: 200 OK — 20 todos, all with "userId": 2
GET {{jsonph}}/todos?userId=2

# GitHub (fixtures only): see api/docs/api-exploration.md, section 3.
# The live requests would be:
#   GET https://api.github.com/users/octocat
#   (and after the room's hourly limit: 403 with x-ratelimit-remaining: 0)
